{# LAN-bound web-UI exposure for a Docker service on daniel-pi, the only Docker host.

   The Pi is LAN-only: a service's UI port is published bound to the host's LAN IP
   ({{ server_ip }}), so it is reachable on the local network and not on the WireGuard tunnel
   or any other interface. There is no Traefik in front of it. Neither cluster node runs
   Docker, so the Docker Traefik-label path (`traefik.yml.j2`, and the `expose_mode` switch
   that chose between it and this one) was deleted in #2385.

   `web_ui_ports_block` emits a complete `ports:` block, so it is for services whose only
   published port is the UI. Invoke it at COLUMN 0 on its own line: it bakes in the
   service-block indentation itself, e.g.

{{ web_ui_ports_block('8096') }}

   No live template calls it (glances was the last, retired 2026-09-18). wg-easy, which also
   publishes its WireGuard UDP port, writes its LAN UI port into its own `ports:` list instead.
#}
{% macro web_ui_ports_block(internal_port) -%}
    ports:
      - "{{ server_ip }}:{{ container_item.port }}:{{ internal_port }}/tcp"
{%- endmacro %}
